.TH ONYM 1 2026-06-07 "Onym 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
onym \- thesaurus and dictionary for GNOME built on WordNet
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B onym
.RI [ word ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Onym
is a thesaurus and dictionary for GNOME, built on WordNet. It shows a word's
meanings grouped by part of speech, with example sentences, then its synonyms,
its antonyms, and the lexical relations that connect it to other words. Every
word on screen is a link, so one lookup leads to the next with a click. Search
is live, with completion as you type and a suggestion when a word is misspelt.
.PP
With no argument, Onym opens to its search field. Given a
.IR word ,
it opens showing that word.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WNSEARCHDIR
The directory holding the WordNet database. When it is unset, Onym falls back to
.IR $WNHOME/dict ,
then to the directory chosen at build time.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/wordnet
The WordNet database, as provided by the
.B wordnet-base
package.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wn (1)
.SH AUTHOR
ursa.nz <code@ursa.nz>
